WEBVTT

NOTE Pregnancy Leave — Who Files What — CFHR training, current as of 10.31.2026. Built from the narration manifest by scripts/build-vtt.mjs and checked against SCRIPT.md.

1
00:00:07.235 --> 00:00:10.363
This is manager training on California pregnancy leave,

2
00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:14.061
current as of October 31st, 2026.

3
00:00:14.061 --> 00:00:16.727
It's a framework, not legal advice.

4
00:00:17.055 --> 00:00:19.615
Here's the calendar from one normal pregnancy.

5
00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:20.712
The job lane:

6
00:00:20.712 --> 00:00:24.491
Pregnancy Disability Leave, then CFRA bonding.

7
00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.466
The pay lane:

8
00:00:25.466 --> 00:00:28.733
State Disability Insurance, then Paid Family Leave.

9
00:00:28.798 --> 00:00:30.505
Every bar starts with paperwork —

10
00:00:30.505 --> 00:00:32.658
and the rule fits in one line.

11
00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:35.056
Leave paperwork goes to the employer.

12
00:00:35.056 --> 00:00:37.531
Pay paperwork goes to EDD.

13
00:00:39.845 --> 00:00:40.576
Now stretch it back

14
00:00:40.576 --> 00:00:42.161
to the day she tells her manager —

15
00:00:42.161 --> 00:00:44.314
about twenty-two weeks before her due date.

16
00:00:44.314 --> 00:00:45.655
Three lanes now:

17
00:00:45.655 --> 00:00:48.971
the employee, her health provider, the employer.

18
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.274
The first document is the employer's:

19
00:00:51.274 --> 00:00:52.900
the Civil Rights Department notice,

20
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.149
Your Rights and Obligations as a Pregnant Employee.

21
00:00:56.197 --> 00:00:57.376
It goes to her as soon

22
00:00:57.376 --> 00:00:59.733
as practicable after she says she's pregnant —

23
00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:03.744
sooner if she asks about accommodation, transfer, or leave.

24
00:01:06.025 --> 00:01:09.153
Next, her PDL request goes to the employer —

25
00:01:09.153 --> 00:01:11.550
at least thirty days ahead when it's foreseeable —

26
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:17.142
and she gets EDD's disability brochure, the DE 2515.

27
00:01:17.205 --> 00:01:20.131
The employer answers within ten calendar days.

28
00:01:20.131 --> 00:01:22.121
If it requires a medical certification,

29
00:01:22.121 --> 00:01:24.316
it asks when she gives notice or within

30
00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:26.897
two business days, and provides the form.

31
00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:30.023
Her provider certifies that she's disabled by pregnancy,

32
00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.038
when it began,

33
00:01:31.038 --> 00:01:33.273
and how long it's expected to last.

34
00:01:33.273 --> 00:01:36.118
Once that's adequate, the employer must accept it —

35
00:01:36.118 --> 00:01:37.902
and may not ask for more.

36
00:01:40.195 --> 00:01:42.104
Her pay runs on a separate track,

37
00:01:42.104 --> 00:01:43.849
straight to EDD.

38
00:01:43.904 --> 00:01:45.692
She files her disability claim —

39
00:01:45.692 --> 00:01:47.520
the DE 2501 —

40
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.853
no later than forty-nine days after her disability begins,

41
00:01:50.853 --> 00:01:52.397
and her provider certifies

42
00:01:52.397 --> 00:01:54.920
it to EDD on the same clock.

43
00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.499
Without that part, the claim isn't complete.

44
00:01:57.499 --> 00:01:59.612
EDD then notifies the employer.

45
00:01:59.612 --> 00:02:02.212
Whenever that notice arrives, the employer has

46
00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:04.429
two working days to send it back.

47
00:02:06.674 --> 00:02:08.787
Bonding needs its own request.

48
00:02:08.787 --> 00:02:11.672
Her CFRA notice goes to the employer —

49
00:02:11.672 --> 00:02:13.907
verbal is enough, if it states the reason —

50
00:02:13.907 --> 00:02:14.720
and she gets

51
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.144
EDD's Paid Family Leave brochure, the DE 2511.

52
00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.024
The employer responds within five business days,

53
00:02:23.024 --> 00:02:26.762
designates the leave as CFRA, and tells her.

54
00:02:26.762 --> 00:02:28.671
Without that notice, it can't designate

55
00:02:28.671 --> 00:02:30.442
the leave after she's back.

56
00:02:30.512 --> 00:02:33.844
At fifty or more employees within seventy-five miles,

57
00:02:33.844 --> 00:02:37.330
federal FMLA notices ride alongside.

58
00:02:43.005 --> 00:02:45.687
At week six, the pay side hands off.

59
00:02:45.687 --> 00:02:49.506
When her last disability payment issues, EDD automatically sends

60
00:02:49.506 --> 00:02:52.619
her the Paid Family Leave claim for new mothers.

61
00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:54.458
She files it within forty-one days

62
00:02:54.458 --> 00:02:56.489
of the date she wants bonding to start.

63
00:02:56.489 --> 00:02:59.659
And the employer returns EDD's notice within two working

64
00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:03.014
days, reporting any wages paid during her leave.

65
00:03:06.295 --> 00:03:07.473
So the bottom line:

66
00:03:07.473 --> 00:03:09.545
leave paperwork goes to the employer.

67
00:03:09.545 --> 00:03:11.659
Pay paperwork goes to EDD.

68
00:03:11.659 --> 00:03:13.243
And the step employers miss most

69
00:03:13.243 --> 00:03:15.337
often is the very first one —

70
00:03:15.438 --> 00:03:17.868
the notice when she tells her manager.

71
00:03:17.919 --> 00:03:19.951
Managers hear it as personal news,

72
00:03:19.951 --> 00:03:21.454
not an HR matter.

73
00:03:21.454 --> 00:03:22.186
Train them to pass

74
00:03:22.186 --> 00:03:24.137
it to HR that same day.
